## Part 2 – CSS Styling and Responsive Design
Part 2 updates the website with an external stylesheet, CSS reset, responsive typography, Flexbox navigation, CSS Grid content layout, visual styling, hover/focus/active states, responsive breakpoints, relative units, responsive image markup and a responsive map.

### Responsive Breakpoints
- Desktop: default two-column Grid layout.
- Tablet: below 60rem, content changes to one column.
- Mobile: below 40rem, navigation and spacing adapt for small screens.
- Small phones: below 25rem, navigation links become full-width.

### Responsive Images
The Home, About Us and Enquiry pages use the picture element together with srcset and sizes. Images use max-width/width rules so they scale with the viewport.

### Testing
Test the five pages using browser Developer Tools at desktop, tablet and mobile sizes. Check navigation, readability, images, forms, map, focus states and horizontal scrolling. Add actual desktop/tablet/mobile screenshots to this README before submission.

